 ## Background
-The technique was introduced as an optimization that terminates resampling along a ray when its accumulated opacity exceeds a user-selected threshold of opaqueness [S1]. It is part of a broader set of optimizations including hierarchical opacity enumeration and adaptive image sampling [S1].
+Early ray termination was described in a paper on volume rendering on scalable shared-memory MIMD architectures [S1]. It was defined as terminating resampling along a ray when its accumulated opacity exceeds a user-selected threshold of opaqueness [S1]. The technique is part of a broader set of optimizations including hierarchical opacity enumeration and adaptive image sampling [S1].
